PRODUCTION READINESS

For the current single-Mac architecture, production readiness means:

    The repository installs from declared dependencies.
    Local secrets and runtime data are not committed.
    Required OAuth scopes are granted.
    The main and dashboard LaunchAgents are running.
    The polling cursor is fresh.
    The WebSocket consumer is active.
    SQLite integrity is healthy.
    There are no overdue failed or dead messages.
    Codex passes a real sample.
    Multica workspace discovery and read-only Issue scanning pass.
    Multica synchronization freshness is healthy when the integration is
    enabled.
    Real group and direct-message tests pass.
    File and mutation capabilities pass separate real tests when enabled.
    The account owner knows how to pause, inspect, restart, and recover the
    service.

This definition does not claim zero failure. It defines a verifiable operating
state and makes remaining single-machine and upstream-service risks explicit.


